<h1>The two tracks</h1>

<p class="lede">
  This site is built as two interleaved tracks through one encyclopedia, an
  idea borrowed with gratitude from Misner, Thorne, and Wheeler's
  <em>Gravitation</em>, the physics textbook famously written that way.
  Track 1 is the course. Track 2 is the depth.
</p>

<h2>Track 1: the spine</h2>

<p>
  One ordered chain of articles that is complete on its own: read only these,
  in order, and you have genuinely learned to speak music. Every spine
  article carries previous and next links, so you can simply keep pressing
  next.
</p>

<ol>
  {%- for a in spine %}
  <li><a href="/concepts/{{ a.slug }}/">{{ a.title }}</a></li>
  {%- endfor %}
</ol>

<h2>Track 2: the paths beyond</h2>

<p>
  Everything off the spine assumes Track 1 but is never required by it.
  Skipping Track 2 costs depth, never continuity. It grows in named reading
  paths, each hanging off particular spine articles, and each path below
  lists what has shipped so far, in reading order. More lands as it is
  written.
</p>

{%- for c in clusters %}
<h3>{{ c.name }}</h3>
<p>{{ c.purpose }}
  Grows out of
  {%- for s in c.hangsOff %}
  <a href="/concepts/{{ s.slug }}/">{{ s.title }}</a>{% if not loop.last %},{% else %}.{% endif %}
  {%- endfor %}
</p>
<ol>
  {%- for a in c.articles %}
  <li><a href="/concepts/{{ a.slug }}/">{{ a.title }}</a></li>
  {%- endfor %}
</ol>
{%- endfor %}
